{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_155013_55d1f4", "exit_code": 0, "text": "**Q1. Can I upgrade from 32 GB to 128 GB myself?**\nYes. You can upgrade the memory yourself. The documentation states that the device supports up to 128 GB and customers may upgrade memory themselves.\n*Source: Section 2: Memory and Storage Upgrades*\n\n**Q2. What warranty comes standard, and can I extend it?**\nThe standard warranty is 3-year on-site, next-business-day. You can extend coverage to 4 or 5 years at purchase or within 90 days of purchase.\n*Source: Section 1: Warranty and Support*\n\n**Q3. How many external monitors can I run from one dock?**\nUp to three external 4K displays at 60 Hz can be run from a single Thunderbolt 5 dock. Alternatively, two external displays at up to 8K 60 Hz are supported.\n*Source: Section 3: Docking and External Displays*\n\n**Q4. What happens if the BIOS is attacked?**\nThe system automatically restores a protected copy of the BIOS at the next boot. The self-healing BIOS continuously checks firmware integrity and restores it if corrupted or attacked.\n*Source: Section 4: Security Features*\n\n**Q5. Is Aurora 14 certified for Ubuntu 24.04?**\nNot covered in the provided documentation\n*Customer should contact support or sales for OS certification details.*", "tokens": {"input": 575, "output": 302, "total": 4696, "cache_read": 3819, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 36177, "timestamp": 1790808650144}